This shelf adds items to an array and reads the first item.
```typescript
class Shelf<T> {
  private values: T[] = [];
  add(value: T): void {
    this.values.push(value);
  }
  first(): T | undefined {
    return this.values[0];
  }
}
const counts = new Shelf<number>();
counts.add(11);
console.log(counts.first());
```
The output is 11. Array position 0 is the first item.
